# 1.0-WORKAROUND(dialog-component-ref-widen)
#
# @gtkx/react's shared `createDialogComponent` factory (used by the
# generated AdwAboutDialog/AdwAlertDialog/AdwDialog/AdwPreferencesDialog/
# AdwShortcutsDialog JSX wrappers) types its returned component's props as
# `PresentedProps<Adw.Dialog>`, where `Adw.Dialog` resolves against
# WHATEVER `@gtkx/gi` store `@gtkx/react` itself sees — in an npm
# workspace that is wherever `@gtkx/react` is hoisted (the workspace
# root), not the per-app `@gtkx/gi` store `gtkx codegen`/`gtkx build`
# freshly generates for each example. Every app whose own store differs
# from the root's (i.e. every app except the root package itself) fails
# `gtkx build`/`gtkx codegen` with "Type checking the generated @gtkx/jsx
# store found 5 error(s)" — a ref-covariance mismatch between the shared
# factory's `Adw.Dialog` and each app's own locally-generated
# `AboutDialog`/`AlertDialog`/`Dialog`/`PreferencesDialog`/`ShortcutsDialog`.
# Reproduced identically for examples/gallery and examples/profile via a
# bare `npx gtkx codegen` (no build step needed). dialog.js's runtime
# implementation is fully duck-typed (`dialog.forceClose()`/
# `dialog.present()`), so this is a `.d.ts`-only defect — widening the
# returned component's props to `any` costs nothing at runtime and
# resolves every one of the 5 diagnostics (they are one bug, not five;
# the plain-name ones just didn't need TS to print the disambiguating
# store paths).
#
# Filed upstream: docs/upstream-gtkx.md (see the gtkx-1-0-migration epic's
# 001-notes.md for the full writeup pending the docs/upstream-gtkx.md
# rewrite in task 002).
#
# Removal condition: @gtkx/react's createDialogComponent stops hardcoding
# a single `@gtkx/gi` store's Dialog type (generic over the component's
# own props, or typed loosely enough to survive multiple per-app stores).
